The chart shows the Richter magnitudes of three earthquakes. Using $A=10^M$, find how many times greater the ground amplitude at Harbour was than at Valley.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(6.8,0);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,7.6);
\foreach \y in {0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7} {\draw (-0.12,\y)--(0,\y); \path (-0.18,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\y$};}
\draw (0.7,0) rectangle (1.7,6);
\draw (2.7,0) rectangle (3.7,3);
\draw (4.7,0) rectangle (5.7,5);
\path (1.2,0) node[below] {Harbour};
\path (3.2,0) node[below] {Valley};
\path (5.2,0) node[below] {Island};
\path (-0.95,3.8) node[rotate=90] {Richter magnitude};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
